CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ two-arg-pack SFINAE constructor selected: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A converting constructor SFINAE-constrained by a decltype that expands a
two-or-more-element pack (declval<A>()...) must be considered: the parser now
preserves the pack-expansion ellipsis on a function-call argument
([temp.variadic]/5) and template_mapt::apply expands it into one argument per
deduced element before the decltype operand is type-checked.  Previously the
ellipsis was discarded, the bare pack reference was rejected, overload
resolution reported "found no match", and construction failed silently (a
vacuous proof).
